Maximise a borderless window through the window manager (Linux).

Segno's main window has no system title bar on Linux (docs/design/menu-bar.md §4). JUCE maximised
such a window by itself: it resized the window to the work area and set its own flag, but only
asked the window manager (_NET_WM_STATE_MAXIMIZED_*) when the native title bar was on. At the next
ConfigureNotify, updateWindowBounds() reads the flag back from _NET_WM_STATE, which the window
manager never set, so the window forgot it was maximised at once: Restore and a double-click
maximised it again (nothing happened), and the window manager couldn't drag it out of maximised.

The request now goes to the window manager for every window, so the state is the window manager's:
Restore returns the earlier size and place, a drag un-maximises, and Super+Up agrees with the
button. A borderless window no longer sizes itself to the work area when maximised: on GNOME that
resize reached the window manager before the request and became the size it restored to. Without
a window manager, Maximise does nothing, as with the native title bar.

The JUCE source has CRLF line endings, and so do this patch's hunks (.gitattributes keeps them).

--- a/modules/juce_gui_basics/native/juce_Windowing_linux.cpp
+++ b/modules/juce_gui_basics/native/juce_Windowing_linux.cpp
@@ -240,15 +240,21 @@
         {
             const auto usingNativeTitleBar = ((getStyleFlags() & windowHasTitleBar) != 0);
 
-            if (usingNativeTitleBar)
-                XWindowSystem::getInstance()->setMaximised (windowH, shouldBeFullScreen);
+            // Segno: ask the window manager for borderless windows too. updateWindowBounds() reads
+            // the state back from _NET_WM_STATE at every ConfigureNotify, so a maximise the window
+            // manager never heard of is forgotten at once, and restoring does nothing.
+            XWindowSystem::getInstance()->setMaximised (windowH, shouldBeFullScreen);
 
+            // Segno: the window manager sizes a borderless window. A size of our own sent with the
+            // request can reach it first and become the size it restores to.
             if (shouldBeFullScreen)
                 r = usingNativeTitleBar ? XWindowSystem::getInstance()->getWindowBounds (windowH, parentWindow)
-                                        : Desktop::getInstance().getDisplays().getDisplayForRect (physicalBounds, true)->userBounds.getSmallestIntegerContainer();
+                                        : Rectangle<int>();
 
             if (! r.isEmpty())
                 setBounds (detail::ScalingHelpers::scaledScreenPosToUnscaled (component, r), shouldBeFullScreen);
+            else
+                fullScreen = shouldBeFullScreen;
 
             component.repaint();
         }
